You are an adversarial reviewer of scientific figures for a research proposal. The attached PNGs are rendered at 2x from SVG and will be displayed about 850 px wide. Try hard to find reasons each figure should not ship. For EACH image, by file order, report: (a) overlapping or colliding text, (b) lines or arrows that cross text or other arrows confusingly, (c) arrows whose direction or endpoints are ambiguous, (d) text too small to read at display size, (e) excess text that belongs in a caption, (f) the one main point and whether a reader gets it in 5 seconds, (g) concrete fixes with coordinates or element names. Then give a verdict per figure: ship / fix / redraw. Focus: README overview figure for a collection of four research proposals. Its single point: a self-improving tool-using agent has four places where self-improvement can go wrong, and each proposal (05 to 08) studies one: 08 the referral or hypothesis given to the agent, 05 the harness code the improver edits, 07 the encoding of tool outputs the VLM reads, 06 the acceptance rule that decides which edits survive. The loop runs clockwise: scores on dev people, improver proposes an edit, acceptance rule, accepted edit updates the harness.. Do not run commands or modify files.

